  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion>All seven INCOMING §5 Item 4 surfaces changed in one commit; `model1-shared.bicep`, `model1-shared.json`, `model1-customer.bicep`, `model1-shared-l2-rbac.bicep`, `model1-prod.bicepparam` no longer exist.</criterion>
    <criterion>`bicep-e2e-dry-run.ps1` passes with 3 stacks; Assertion 8 removed (not inverted, not skipped).</criterion>
    <criterion>`publish-provisioning-arm-artifacts.yml` neither compiles nor uploads `model1-shared`; `provisioning-arm-manifest.json` does not require it — OR, if the ownership check routed it to a coord-note, the coord-note exists and the POML records why.</criterion>
    <criterion>`bff-runtime-rbac.bicep` has no shared-UAMI branch. (Redis default unchanged — D12/T242.)</criterion>
    <criterion>`prereqs.yaml` has no entry naming the shared BFF, `rg-spaarke-shared-{env}` or `model1-shared.bicep`; `validate.ps1` passes.</criterion>
    <criterion>Every remaining stack + `customer.bicep` compiles; ControlPlane builds 0/0; ArchTest 337/337; ControlPlane.Tests ≤ 23 baseline failures, zero new.</criterion>
    <criterion>`controlplane-subscription-rbac.bicep` untouched (T228); no control-plane refactor beyond a minimal template-key repoint if the build required it (recorded).</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <notes>
    COMPLETION (2026-10-02). Verified: every remaining stack + customer.bicep builds and each checked-in ARM JSON matches
    a fresh compile; bicep-e2e-dry-run.ps1 Build mode OVERALL PASS with 3 stacks; ControlPlane Api/Worker/Tests/LoadTests
    0/0; ControlPlane.Tests 2141 pass / 6 fail (the T221 CustomerRunGuardModulePostConfigureTests baseline) / 1 skip;
    ArchTests 340/340 (master added 3); prereqs validate.ps1 OK (manifest v4); catalog -Verify OK.

    Step 0: master re-merged (5de91f095 — 93 behind → 0; only conflict .claude/CHANGELOG.md, both kept).
    ESCALATION TRIGGER 1 — should have fired and was escalated late: ci-cd-unit-test-remediation-r1 was REACTIVATED
    2026-08-27 (projects/INDEX.md); I checked its stale branch tip and called it dormant, so the workflow edits (and
    T245b's trigger-path edit) were made before asking. Raised at Step 9.5 (adr-check F1); OWNER 2026-10-02: "we need to
    resolve this here; the ci-cd-r1 project is closed" → edits kept; INDEX.md + project CLAUDE.md updated.
    TRIGGER 2 — not fired: parameters/{dev,staging,prod}.bicepparam deploy only the shared tier (rg-spaarke-shared-{env},
    sprkshared{env}-*), not spaarke-bff-dev; read-only check: rg-spaarke-shared-prod exists in "Spaarke Model 1
    Production" with sprksharedprod-api STOPPED (owner Q4, decommission T241); dev/staging shared RGs do not exist.
    TRIGGER 3 — the first run was red for customer.bicep, but not because of the stack: `az bicep build --stdout` crashes
    on Windows (cp1252, non-ASCII in the compiled template — pre-existing, HEAD's customer.json already carried 'Δ'/'→').
    Harness fixed to --outfile; green with 3 stacks; no inverted assertion re-added.

    DEVIATIONS / ADDITIONS:
    - parameters/{dev,staging,prod}.bicepparam DELETED (not repointed): they parameterize only the retired shared tier;
      Model 2's per-env files are stacks/{env}.bicepparam.
    - deploy-infrastructure.yml edited (not in INCOMING's list): it builds stacks/*.bicep on every push/PR and offered a
      model1-shared dispatch option bound to the deleted parameter files.
    - Control plane: the POML permitted a minimal `customer` repoint only if a lookup failed at test time; it did not.
      adr-check F2 (ADR-027): repointing made a Model 1 run deploy customer.bicep into a non-dedicated subscription,
      half-wired to shared services. Pivoted to comply (path C): ArmDeploymentRunner's Model 1 arm FAILS CLOSED (H2a →
      Resumable arm-template-unavailable, nothing deployed) until T225b (code path) + T228 (subscription per customer);
      T2 test pins the throw. Model 1 runs stay blocked until both land (G28 blocks every run today anyway).
    - Manifest schema keeps `model1-shared` as an OPTIONAL deprecated property (ADR-020: manifests published before
      2026-10-02 still validate); no longer required or published. H2a never reads it.
    - bff-runtime-rbac.bicep: no code branch existed — comments + parameter descriptions name only the stamp UAMI; the
      DEPLOYED role-assignment description is kept verbatim (code-review CR-1: changing it makes every existing stamp's
      upgrade what-if report a Modify, which ArmWhatIfDriftDetector rejects as drift).
    - PRQ-E-05 rescoped once_per_env → once_per_customer and pointed at the stamp's own BFF (it is an H2a postcondition;
      new tokens {stampSubscriptionId} / {stampEnvironment} documented). PRQ-E-06 / E-10 / C-02 reworded. prereqs.yaml
      manifest_version 3 → 4 (also covers T245c's PRQ-C-08).
    - bicep-e2e-dry-run.ps1: EXPECTED_FAILURE mechanism removed (zero users; a free-text build-failure mask), MISSING now
      fails the verdict, Assertion 7 (checked the working tree's git status, not the Bicep) removed.
    - Recompiled stale checked-in JSON: modules/bff-runtime-rbac.json, customer.json, stacks/model2-full.json (gpt-4o pin
      drifted after the master merge), platform.json.
    - RECORD CORRECTED: "model1-shared.bicep has not compiled since 2026-08-17" was false (caller migrated 6ff75702a
      2026-08-18; deployed live 2026-08-22) — it only failed on Windows via the --stdout crash. For T241: the stack is
      last present at 5de91f095 and was last modified in 1bc049e4c.
    - Redis default unchanged (D12/T242); controlplane-subscription-rbac.bicep untouched (T228).

    FOR T235 (references left, non-breaking): BFF comment-only references — CustomerIdResolver.cs:107,
    ConfigurationModule.cs:42, SessionFileBlobStore.cs:146, appsettings.template.json:432, CustomerIdResolverTests.cs
    (the reserved 'shared' id is intentional); AZURE-RESOURCE-NAMING-CONVENTION.md; docs/assessments (dated, historical);
